  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Find all solutions to \((x+5)(2x−3)=0\). Explain or show your reasoning.</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solutions to the equation and your reasoning.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x=-5\) and \(x=\frac {3}{2}\)</para>
    <para>By the zero product property, either \(x+5=0\) or \(2x−3=0\), so \(x=-5\) and \(x=\frac {3}{2}\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
